[Music]  you know how when you're in a store the  cashier will often ask if you'd like to  be emailed to your receipt  this is a pretty shameless attempt to  secure a really valuable piece of  information your email address it's the  anchor for much of your online identity  and lets brands tally the data they  might have about you with stuff they  might be able to source elsewhere but  crucially it also lets them forge a  direct relationship with you the  customer rather than having to pay for  advertising on a social media platform  on a television screen or a billboard it  can instead send an email straight to  your inbox every week  that lets it promote its latest  offerings give you discounts all without  having to pay for additional ads  the same goes for news organizations  rather than having to fight for an  audience on twitter or facebook every  time a story is published it can instead  send a newsletter with the summary of  the day's news that might be  particularly personal to you the average  american received emails from four news  organizations a week in 2020 and about  the same proportion of people received  their news from email as they do from  mobile notifications  that's why we've seen an explosion in  newsletters and email marketing over the  past few years they let brands evade the  tech gatekeepers and forge direct  relationships with their audience but a  lot of the value resides in knowing  quite how many people are opening those  emails you might have a hundred thousand  subscribers but if you can show that  forty percent of those are opening the  message every week it makes it easier to  attract a sponsor for your newsletter  the same stands for email marketing if  you know how many people are opening the  message you can gauge how effective the  campaign might be  so how do they know you've actually  opened the message well most of these  emails arrive just as blocks of text  with no pictures in order to get the  pictures it will ping a server  download them into the email and in  pinging the server it tells the brand  that you have opened the email as well  as perhaps giving useful information  such as your rough location and what  sort of device you're opening the  message on the unassuming newsletter is  a bit of a trojan horse now as part of a  broader crackdown on advertising  technology apple introduced a tool in  2021 it caused male privacy protection  that system downloads all the images for  your emails irrespective of whether you  open them or not makes it a lot harder  for the sender of the email to know who  has indeed opened their messages and  that's a big deal because about half of  all emails are opened through an apple  app  it's prompted big changes to both the  newsletter and email marketing  industries  rather than being largely subsidized by  advertising newsletters are increasingly  paid subscriber affairs the new york  times has taken many of its top  newsletters behind the paywall meaning  that it only goes to people paying for a  subscription and email marketers are  working harder to get you to click  through their content to an outside  website if you've clicked on it that  means you've opened the message  it's made apple into a gatekeeper of  your inbox long the preserve of google  its gmail service has for a long time  filtered your emails into primary social  and promotional inboxes those last two  are sort of a purgatory between the  heaven of your normal inbox and the hell  of your spam folder and don't get as  many eyeballs  in the data wars even your inbox is a  fierce battleground  [Music]

